{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXCIFQuadtree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rectangle is split into four equal quadrants, and each quadrant again, and each element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hangs on the smallest cell that wholly contains its box, so a box that straddles a cell’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"centre line stays at that cell (Kedem, “The Quad-CIF Tree”, 1982). A search visits only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cells that meet its region. Cells are made on the way down to an element and freed when their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtree empties. Cells at depth 24 have no quadrants, so smaller boxes stay there."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var plan = MXCIFQuadtree<String>(bounds: BoundingBox(lower: [0, 0], upper: [100, 100]))","plan.insert(\"hall\", in: BoundingBox(lower: [10, 10], upper: [60, 20]))","plan.insert(\"office\", in: BoundingBox(lower: [10, 20], upper: [30, 40]))","plan.insert(\"garden\", in: BoundingBox(lower: [70, 70], upper: [90, 90]))","plan.items(containing: [20, 15]).map(\\.element)          \/\/ [\"hall\"]","plan.items(overlapping: BoundingBox(lower: [25, 18], upper: [35, 25])).count   \/\/ 2","plan.overlappingPairs().count                            \/\/ 1: the hall and the office touch"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Boxes include their faces, so two that touch overlap. A box whose lower edge lies on a centre","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"line belongs to the upper quadrant. The elements and their boxes are a sequence, in no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"particular order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"An MX-CIF quadtree: elements over boxes in a rectangle, which finds those overlapping a box,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"those containing a point, and every pair that overlaps, and takes insertions and removals as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the boxes move.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/init(bounds:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/bounds","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/count","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/isEmpty"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/insert(_:checkedIn:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/insert(_:in:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/items(containing:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/items(overlapping:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/overlappingPairs()","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree\/remove(_:in:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/Spa